    <string name="l_frozen">Frozen by Boox</string>
    <string name="l_frozen_explain">Boox froze this app, so Android won’t start it. Boox’s own home unfreezes an app when you open it there. BooxUltimatum can do the same when Shizuku is running, which you can set up under Device › Access. You can also turn the app on in Boox’s App Freeze page, then open it again.</string>
    <string name="l_frozen_explain_shizuku">Boox froze this app. Opening it here unfreezes it first, as Boox’s own home does. BooxUltimatum freezes it again about a minute after you return to this home screen, or when the tablet locks.</string>
    <string name="l_frozen_page">Open App Freeze</string>
    <string name="l_about_home">About BooxUltimatum home</string>
    <string name="l_about_home_text">The recent apps screen, Boox gestures, the NaviBall and EInkWise stay with Boox, so they work the same under BooxUltimatum home. You can restore the Boox home from BooxUltimatum › Suite › Home screen, in one tap with Shizuku.</string>
